<title>USA: CME March lumber falls sharply, mills lower prices.</title>
<headline>CME March lumber falls sharply, mills lower prices.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME March lumber futures were sharply lower in late trade on selling sparked by mills lowering asking prices in the cash market as cold weather slowed demand across the United States, floor traders said.</p>
<p>Selling was scattered.</p>
<p>At 1256 CST March lumber was off $9.00 at $403.00 per thousand board feet.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
